# build output
/bin/
/dist/
# The generated website. Built by make site, uploaded to S3, never committed:
# it is entirely derived from README.md, docs/ and site/.
/dist-site/
# anchored to the repo root so it does not match the cmd/perfuse package
/perfuse
/perfuse.exe

# local state
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/data/

# Never commit clinical data. Real HL7 is protected health information; the only
# messages in this repository are hand-written synthetic fixtures in testdata.
*.hl7
!**/testdata/**/*.hl7
*.hl7.gz
*.er7
corpus/
/testdata/corpus/
**/corpus/

# front end
web/node_modules/
web/.vite/
# internal/web/dist is committed on purpose: it lets `go build` work on a
# checkout with no Node installed. Rebuild it with `make web`.

# The WebAssembly playground, 26 MB, is committed under internal/web/dist and
# embedded in the binary. Only the staging copy under web/public is ignored.
#
# This reversed an earlier decision, and the reversal is recorded because the two
# halves of it contradicted each other for a while and nothing noticed.
#
# The original reasoning was sound on its own terms: the playground exists so that
# somebody who has NOT installed Perfuse can try it in a browser, anybody who has
# installed it does not need it, and embedding it takes the binary from 34 MB to
# 61 MB. So it was ignored here and meant to live on a public website.
#
# But the interface ships a Playground tab, and internal/web/embed.go names
# dist/wasm in its embed directive precisely because omitting it left that tab
# broken in every build: the browser asked for the module, the SPA fallback
# answered with index.html, and the script would not execute. Two files therefore
# documented opposite decisions, and because a go:embed pattern that matches
# nothing is a compile error, the repository could not be built by anybody who
# cloned it - `go install` included. That went unnoticed because the only machine
# that ever built it already had the untracked file sitting there.
#
# Resolved in favour of the tab working. If the binary size matters more later,
# the honest fix is to serve the module gzipped - Go WebAssembly compresses about
# four to one, so roughly 7 MB - rather than to ship a tab that cannot run.
web/public/wasm/

# editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Playwright end-to-end artefacts. The tests are committed; their output is not.
web/test-results/
web/e2e-report/
web/e2e/.auth/
web/e2e/.state.json
# The run lock, which names the pid of whichever run holds the suite. Per-machine and per-run, never shared.
web/e2e/.run.lock

# Local assistant and editor tooling, not part of the product.
.kiro/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Runtime state, created by the server as it runs.
pid
perfuse-settings.yaml
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
data/
archive/
claims/
